[00:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This is an amazing feeling, but almost no one\'s doing it. We think it\'s because it\'s too expensive and it\'s too hard to do. We wanted to fix that and today I\'ll share what I\'ve been up to. We\'ve been doing this for almost 10'

[00:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'years and it\'s changed a lot. The wings were much smaller then and we needed a boat to pull us around. But everything changed when I saw someone doing it all by themselves. No boat, no rope. Launching is the hardest part, so we'

[00:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tried many different ways to make it easier and failed at each one of them. So we created a contest. Anyone who could do this for 1 minute earned themselves a hat. While 900 people have earned their hats, many, many more have given up.'

[00:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And this sport is expensive. Top setups cost as much as $4,000 and when you build a setup, you have to select each component and make the appropriate trade-offs.'

[00:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'But the trade-offs aren\'t obvious until you\'ve tried many. So I set out to create the product I wish I had when I started. More affordable, easier to use, and with all the right components, so'

[01:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you don\'t have to choose them. The Swiss foil brand Indiana Paddle and Surf had the same idea. So we did it together. The foil we created is easier to launch'

[01:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'from land, whether it\'s a dock, a rock, or even a boat. It can take off from a standstill, which makes it easier because you don\'t need to run up to it.'

[01:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The wing was designed for taking a ride on the wakes of passing boats. So it\'s fast enough to chase down a boat and maneuverable enough so you can enjoy the ride.'

[01:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'It also fits in a backpack, so you can go wherever there\'s water. And it\'s fully compatible with Indiana\'s products, so you can grow into whatever discipline calls to you next.'

[01:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This is what I would have wanted when I began this sport. But we hadn\'t made it easy enough. Many struggled to learn the start, and'

[02:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'my son and his friends were no different. I saw a foil with a handle, so gave it a try. &gt;&gt; [screaming] &gt;&gt; The handle gave them the confidence to'

[02:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'commit and keep trying without fear. With each try, they got better and better. After a few hours, they earned their hats. I had never imagined anyone could earn a'

[02:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hat in just a few hours. After a few sessions, my son had mastered the dock start, learned to surf behind our jet ski, and even launch from it. He was hopping from dock to dock and'

[02:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'even managed to pump for 8 minutes. It took me years of testing and riding hundreds of foils to figure out what good looked like, but only one afternoon to see what I\'d been missing.'

[03:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And today you can pre-order this product with or without the removable handle. This has been a passion project. I wanted a more affordable foil that performed like the best.'

[03:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'But it evolved into something so much more. An opportunity to give everyone a chance to fly. [music] I can\'t promise you\'ll earn a hat on day one, but when you get to a minute, I can promise you that amazing feeling of'

[03:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'accomplishing something really hard. And it doesn\'t get any better than that.'
